Modified by TOFI: the SKILL.md rules on formulas, number formats, function
choice for LibreOffice, openpyxl cautions and financial-model conventions were
rewritten from the upstream SKILL.md. scripts/xlsx_recalc.py is new code that
follows the idea of upstream scripts/recalc.py (LibreOffice calculates a copy,
a report names the error cells); no upstream code is included. Differences:
the TOFI script keeps formulas by saving LibreOffice's calculated copy, exits
non-zero when any cell holds an error (upstream exits 0 with errors found),
and never edits its input. The upstream advice to open a workbook with
data_only=True and save it is not carried over, because saving that workbook
destroys its formulas. The upstream office/ helpers, XML schemas and the
LibreOffice socket shim are not included.
